WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.464 --> 00:00:13.560
Makeup changes by venue mainly because each place has different lighting and environmental conditions.

2
00:00:13.896 --> 00:00:24.408
Hotels have high ceilings, wide spaces, and dazzling lighting — makeup that's too natural can make you fade into the background or look plain.

3
00:00:24.744 --> 00:00:34.776
So matching the hotel's atmosphere with a radiant, luxurious "rich makeup" that makes the skin glow like a jewel helps establish your presence.

4
00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:43.824
Churches and cathedrals, on the other hand, tend to have dimmer, cooler daylight-toned lighting suited for worship.

5
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.864
Without adjustment, this can make your complexion look dull,

6
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:58.224
so a pink-toned base and dewy, "glass skin" finish help keep you looking fresh and bright under that lighting.

7
00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:04.680
For outdoor and botanical garden weddings, strong natural light and wind are the key factors.

8
00:01:05.016 --> 00:01:16.416
Sunlight draws moisture from the skin, accentuating fine lines and causing sweat, so a highly hydrating base and smudge-proof waterproof techniques are essential.

9
00:01:16.752 --> 00:01:26.640
Strong hair-setting techniques are also needed so a breeze doesn't ruin your style, keeping you photo-ready throughout.

10
00:01:26.976 --> 00:01:34.968
This kind of venue-tailored makeup is what makes the decisive difference in completing a wedding parent's elegance.
